# Local scratch — never published
control/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Live handoff state is machine-local; the config is not
.handoff/HANDOFF.md
.handoff/processed_*

# A test instrument, not a rule: T-288's probe, which T-295 deletes when it takes the
# reading. `.claude/rules/` itself is deliberately NOT ignored - whether this repository
# should track a rule file at all is T-295's decision, and ignoring the directory would
# take it. `git add -A` published this one before anyone chose; hence the line.
.claude/rules/t-288-probe.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# Corpus knowledgebase — full-fidelity extraction of the owner's private notes.
# Local-only by construction: it contains client and personal data and must never publish.
.kb/
.assets-cache/

# Presenter builds. A second artifact from the same specification, carrying the speaker notes
# DS-088 keeps out of a shipped deck (T-211 section 3, T-213). It is generated beside the deck
# because that is where a presenter wants it, and ignored here because it must never be committed:
# `check_all.py` fails any tracked `.html` it has no entry for, so a committed one would go red -
# correctly, and one release later than this line does.
*-presenter.html

# Printed output. The repository keeps the script and the numbers, never the artefact (R6),
# and a printed PDF also carries whatever the print dialog put in its header.
examples/*.pdf
